        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the interquartile range.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "12 minutes.",
          "worked": "Omit the median. The lower and upper groups each contain 10 values, so average the middle two values of each group.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q_1&=\\frac{29+31}{2}\\\\Q_1&=30\\text{ minutes}\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{42+42}{2}\\\\Q_3&=42\\text{ minutes}\\\\\\text{IQR}&=42-30\\\\\\text{IQR}&=12\\text{ minutes}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use the information to construct a boxplot.",
